DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_5350_769F';
<p>5350_769f</p> <h4>Two-Point Test Cross Problem</h4><p>A test cross is a way to explore the relationship between genes and their respective alleles. It is a useful tool for genetic mapping and deciphering the inheritance of traits. Specifically, a two-point test cross examines two (2) genes at the same time to learn about their assortment in gamete formation.</p><p>A standard two-point test cross involves crossing a heterozygous organism for both genes with an organism that is homozygous recessive for both genes</p> <p>For this problem, a test cross using a fruit fly (<i>Drosophila melanogaster</i>) heterozygous for two genes was conducted to understand their genetic interactions.</p><h6>Characteristics of Recessive Phenotypes</h6><p><ul><li><strong><span style="color: #914610;">Gene P</span></strong> is affiliated with the '<span style="color: #914610;"><i>prickly</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #914610;">Gene P</span> is covered with sharp bristles, giving it a spiky texture.</li> <li><strong><span style="color: #007047;">Gene X</span></strong> is associated with the '<span style="color: #007047;"><i>xanthic</i></span>' phenotype. A fruit fly that is homozygous recessive for <span style="color: #007047;">Gene X</span> has a fluorescent bright yellow coloring.</li> </ul></p><table style="border-collapse: collapse; border: 2px solid black;"><tr><th align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Phenotype</span></th><th colspan="2" align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Genotypes</span></th><th align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">Progeny<br/>Count</span></th></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">prickly, xanthic</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffe4d6; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">p</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #d0f5dd; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">x</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">1,807</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">prickly</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffe4d6; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">p</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #007047;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">13,154</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">xanthic</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #914610;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #d0f5dd; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #000000;">x</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">13,225</span></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;">&nbsp;<span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;"><i>wildtype</i></span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #914610;">+</span></td><td align="center" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #f8f8f8; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: large; color: #007047;">+</span></td><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">1,814</span></td></tr><tr><th colspan="3" align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #cccccc; padding: 10px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">TOTAL =</span></th><td align="right" style="border: 1px solid black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 5px;"><span style="font-size: medium; color: #000000;">30,000</span></td></tr></table><p>The resulting phenotypes are summarized in the table above.</p> <h6>Question</h6> <p>With the progeny data from the table, <strong>calculate the genetic distance between the two genes,</strong> expressing your answer in centimorgans (cM)</p>
PROMPT_5350_769F
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_1';
<sup>(1,807 + 1,814)</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = <sup>3,621</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = 0.1207 = <strong>12.07 cM</strong>
LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_2';
<sup>(1,807 + 13,154)</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = <sup>14,961</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = 0.4987 = <strong>49.87 cM</strong>
LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_3';
<sup>(1,807 + 13,225)</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = <sup>15,032</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = 0.5011 = <strong>50.11 cM</strong>
LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_4';
<sup>(1,814 + 13,154)</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = <sup>14,968</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = 0.4989 = <strong>49.89 cM</strong>
LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_5';
<sup>(1,814 + 13,225)</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = <sup>15,039</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = 0.5013 = <strong>50.13 cM</strong>
LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_5
$choice_6 = <<'LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_6';
<sup>(13,154 + 13,225)</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = <sup>26,379</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = 0.8793 = <strong>87.93 cM</strong>
LITERAL_5350_769F_CHOICE_6
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_5350_769F_CORRECT_1';
<sup>(1,807 + 1,814)</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = <sup>3,621</sup>/<sub>30,000</sub> = 0.1207 = <strong>12.07 cM</strong>
LITERAL_5350_769F_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5, $choice_6);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
